          "content": {
            "size": 69159,
            "compression": 56359,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"entities\":{\"bibs\":{\"S114C1807982\":{\"id\":\"S114C1807982\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1807982\",\"title\":\"AI for Life\",\"subtitle\":\"100+ Ways to Use Artificial Intelligence to Make your Life Easier, More Productive ... and More Fun!\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"006.3 QUI\",\"description\":\"\\\"Every day, it seems like there's a new AI tool on the market and a new, complicated way to use it. But what if you could use AI to make your life easier without the complications? In AI for Life, AI expert and creator of @SmartWorkAI offers over 100 ideas and ready-to-use prompts to get AI beginners started using the technology to actually improve their lives. Beginning with a primer on the basics-including an overview of the popular and free AI tools-you will learn expert-tested tips and tricks to get the most out of your AI use, such as layering prompts to dive deeper into an initial response or asking for the output in different formats. Packed with practical how-to information, AI for Life is the must-have guide for using generative AI to make life easier, more productive, more organized, and more fun!\\\"-- Provided by publisher.\",\"genreForm\":[],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Artificial intelligence\",\"Artificial intelligence Data processing\"],\"authors\":[\"Quillian, Celia\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781507223390/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781507223390/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781507223390/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781507223390\",\"9781507223406\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":\"First Adams Media trade paperback edition\",\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Artificial Intelligence -- Data Processing\"],\"groupKey\":\"ai_for_life_100_ways_to_use_artificial_intelligence_to_make_your_life_easier_more_productive_and_mor�quillian_celia�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1807982\",\"rating\":{\"averageRating\":54,\"totalCount\":10}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":true,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1807982\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"NA\",\"status\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":0,\"totalCopies\":3,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"UNAVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1728768\":{\"id\":\"S114C1728768\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1728768\",\"title\":\"Cloud Security for Dummies\",\"subtitle\":\"\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"004.6782 COO\",\"description\":\"Cloud technology has changed the way we approach technology. It's also given rise to a new set of security challenges caused by bad actors who seek to exploit vulnerabilities in a digital infrastructure. You can put the kibosh on these hackers and their dirty deeds by hardening the walls that protect your data.\",\"genreForm\":[],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Cloud computing Security measures\",\"Computer networks Security measures\",\"Computer security\"],\"authors\":[\"Coombs, Ted\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2022\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781119790464/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781119790464/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781119790464/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781119790464\",\"1119790468\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[{\"name\":\"--For dummies\",\"volume\":null,\"sortName\":\"--for dummies\",\"volumeNumber\":null}],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Cloud Computing -- Security Measures\",\"Computer Networks -- Security Measures\",\"Computer Security\"],\"groupKey\":\"cloud_security_for_dummies�coombs_ted�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1728768\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":true,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1728768\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"NA\",\"status\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":0,\"totalCopies\":4,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"UNAVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1312885\":{\"id\":\"S114C1312885\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1312885\",\"title\":\"The Downsized Veggie Garden\",\"subtitle\":\"How to Garden Small Wherever You Live, Whatever your Space\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"635 COP\",\"description\":\"Small is beautiful, and integrating a small, easy-to-manage garden into hectic everyday life is easy. In The Downsized Veggie Garden, low maintenance is the mantra. And so is making smart, creative use of the space we have -- whether it's outdoors, indoors, in-ground, in containers, on a balcony railing...or even going vertical. Garden expert Kate Copsey takes the reader season-by-season, plant-by-plant, with essential tips about soil, seed-starting, plant choices, non-chemical fertilizing, watering, choosing the right containers, veggie garden planning and planting, and much more. This fully illustrated book is a one-stop guide for the beginner gardener or the downsizing gardener.\",\"genreForm\":[],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Vegetable gardening\",\"Small gardens\"],\"authors\":[\"Copsey, Kate\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2016\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781943366002/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781943366002/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781943366002/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781943366002\",\"1943366004\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Vegetable Gardening\",\"Small Gardens\"],\"groupKey\":\"downsized_veggie_garden_how_to_garden_small_wherever_you_live_whatever_your_space�copsey_kate�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1312885\",\"rating\":{\"averageRating\":81,\"totalCount\":8}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":false,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1312885\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"NA\",\"status\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":0,\"totalCopies\":1,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"UNAVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1784208\":{\"id\":\"S114C1784208\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1784208\",\"title\":\"How AI Works\",\"subtitle\":\"From Sorcery to Science\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"006.3 KNE\",\"description\":\"\\\"An accessible, straightforward guide that demystifies Artificial Intelligence for a general audience without the use of complex math or technical jargon. Covers the fundamentals, from classical models and neural networks to the large language models leading today's AI revolution\\\"-- Provided by publisher.\",\"genreForm\":[\"Popular Works\"],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Artificial intelligence Popular works\",\"Neural networks (Computer science) Popular works\"],\"authors\":[\"Kneusel, Ronald T.\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781718503724/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781718503724/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781718503724/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781718503724\",\"9781718503731\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Artificial Intelligence -- Popular Works\",\"Neural Networks (Computer Science) -- Popular Works\"],\"groupKey\":\"how_ai_works_from_sorcery_to_science�kneusel_ronald_t�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1784208\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":false,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1784208\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"NA\",\"status\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":0,\"totalCopies\":1,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"UNAVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1784224\":{\"id\":\"S114C1784224\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1784224\",\"title\":\"Learning Data Science\",\"subtitle\":\"Data Wrangling, Exploration, Visualization, and Modeling With Python\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"006.312 LAU\",\"description\":\"\\\"As an aspiring data scientist, you appreciate why organizations rely on data for important decisions--whether it's for companies designing websites, cities deciding how to improve services, or scientists discovering how to stop the spread of disease. And you want the skills required to distill a messy pile of data into actionable insights. We call this the data science lifecycle: the process of collecting, wrangling, analyzing, and drawing conclusions from data. [This] is the first book to cover foundational skills in both programming and statistics that encompass this entire lifecycle. It's aimed at those who wish to become data scientists or who already work with data scientists, and at data analysts who wish to cross the 'technical/nontechnical' divide. If you have a basic knowledge of Python programming, you'll learn how to work with data using industry-standard tools like pandas\\\"-- Publisher description.\",\"genreForm\":[],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Python (Computer program language)\",\"Data mining\",\"Python (Langage de programmation)\",\"Exploration de données (Informatique)\",\"Data mining\",\"Python (Computer program language)\"],\"authors\":[\"Lau, Sam\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2023\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781098113001/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781098113001/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781098113001/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781098113001\",\"1098113004\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":\"First edition\",\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Python (Computer Program Language)\",\"Data Mining\",\"Python (Langage De Programmation)\",\"Exploration De Données (Informatique)\",\"Data Mining\",\"Python (Computer Program Language)\"],\"groupKey\":\"learning_data_science_data_wrangling_exploration_visualization_and_modeling_with_python�lau_sam�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1784224\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":false,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1784224\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"NA\",\"status\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":0,\"totalCopies\":1,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"UNAVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1788468\":{\"id\":\"S114C1788468\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1788468\",\"title\":\"Mastering AI\",\"subtitle\":\"A Survival Guide to Our Superpowered Future\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"006.3 KAH\",\"description\":\"\\\"A Fortune magazine journalist draws on his expertise and extensive contacts among the companies and scientists at the forefront of artificial intelligence to offer dramatic predictions of AI's impact over the next decade, from reshaping our economy and the way we work, learn, and create to unknitting our social fabric, jeopardizing our democracy, and fundamentally altering the way we think. Within the next five years, Jeremy Kahn predicts, AI will disrupt almost every industry and enterprise, with vastly increased efficiency and productivity. It will restructure the workforce, making AI copilots a must for every knowledge worker. It will revamp education, meaning children around the world can have personal, portable tutors. It will revolutionize health care, making individualized, targeted pharmaceuticals more affordable. It will compel us to reimagine how we make art, compose music, and write and publish books. The potential of generative AI to extend our skills, talents, and creativity as humans is undeniably exciting and promising. But while this new technology has a bright future, it also casts a dark and fearful shadow. AI will provoke pervasive, disruptive, potentially devastating knock-on effects. Leveraging his unrivaled access to the leaders, scientists, futurists, and others who are making AI a reality, Kahn will argue that if not carefully designed and vigilantly regulated AI will deepen income inequality, depressing wages while imposing winner-take-all markets across much of the economy. AI risks undermining democracy, as truth is overtaken by misinformation, racial bias, and harmful stereotypes. Continuing a process begun by the internet, AI will rewire our brains, likely inhibiting our ability to think critically, to remember, and even to get along with one another--unless we all take decisive action to prevent this from happening.\\\"-- Publisher's description.\",\"genreForm\":[],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Artificial intelligence\",\"Artificial intelligence Social aspects\",\"Artificial intelligence Political aspects\",\"Artificial intelligence Forecasting\"],\"authors\":[\"Kahn, Jeremy\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781668053324/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781668053324/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781668053324/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781668053324\",\"1668053322\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Artificial Intelligence -- Social Aspects\",\"Artificial Intelligence -- Political Aspects\",\"Artificial Intelligence -- Forecasting\"],\"groupKey\":\"mastering_ai_a_survival_guide_to_our_superpowered_future�kahn_jeremy�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1788468\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":false,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1788468\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"OTHER\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":1,\"totalCopies\":4,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"AVAILABLE_IN_BRANCH\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"AVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1794755\":{\"id\":\"S114C1794755\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1794755\",\"title\":\"Microsoft Copilot Pro\",\"subtitle\":\"Step by Step\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"005.446 CRO\",\"description\":\"Copilot Pro enables you to be more creative and productive, but using generative AI requires a whole new way of thinking most users try once or twice, get poor results and give up. This book teaches them what they don't know and helps them get started with the right skills. Copilot Pro adds generative AI experiences into the most used Microsoft applications, Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, Excel, and OneNote, enabling users to be more productive and creative by generating first drafts, editing and improving their work, easily understanding and finding pieces of information in large documents, and gaining new insights. It also allows users to generate text and images in a browser and via a mobile app, using the latest AI models. This is a completely new way of thinking and workinglike having your own personal \\\"enthusiastic intern\\\" working side by side with you every day to take on the mundane and time-consuming tasks, freeing you up for more interesting and creative work. Generative AI has been everywhere in the media, with a huge hype cycle, but most everyday workers don't understand how it can be applied to their day-to-day work in a practical and transformative way.\",\"genreForm\":[],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Microsoft Windows (Computer file)\",\"Microsoft Office\",\"Natural language processing (Computer science)\",\"Artificial intelligence\",\"Chatbots\",\"Business Computer programs\"],\"authors\":[\"Crosbie, Lisa\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780135369425/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780135369425/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780135369425/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9780135369425\",\"0135369428\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[{\"name\":\"Step by step\",\"volume\":null,\"sortName\":\"step by step\",\"volumeNumber\":null}],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Microsoft Windows (Computer File)\",\"Microsoft Office\",\"Natural Language Processing (Computer Science)\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Chatbots\",\"Business -- Computer Programs\"],\"groupKey\":\"microsoft_copilot_pro_step_by_step�crosbie_lisa�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1794755\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":true,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1794755\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"OTHER\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":1,\"totalCopies\":4,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"AVAILABLE_IN_BRANCH\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"AVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1671468\":{\"id\":\"S114C1671468\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1671468\",\"title\":\"Money From Nothing\",\"subtitle\":\"Or, Why We Should Stop Worrying About Debt and Learn to Love the Federal Reserve\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"330 HOC\",\"description\":\"\\\"When the government decides to spend money, it simply creates the necessary funds for itself - as if out of thin air. That's how we pay for interstate highways, post offices, wars, social services, and economic stimulus packages. If it's that easy to make money...can't we all get more of it? Absolutely. And we should. So argue financial regulation expert Robert Hockett and best-selling philosopher Aaron James in this eye-opening, irreverent, and inspiring exploration of what the dollar really is. And better still, they show how we can build an economy that works for everybody without unwanted taxes and added regulations. In the process, we learn how disingenuous the political rhetoric surrounding inflation can be, how the demonized concept of the deficit is really just another way of tallying our collective national wealth, and how a strong central bank could free us from the abuses of private banking. With broad historical background and ambitious yet practical institutional proposals, Hockett and James offer a new vision of public finance - people's banking for a people's economy. Armed with this new outlook, we can even stop worrying debt and learn to love a strong, accountable, and transparent Federal Reserve as a cornerstone of our democracy.\\\"--Amazon.\",\"genreForm\":[],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Federal Reserve banks\",\"Monetary policy United States\",\"Economics United States\"],\"authors\":[\"Hockett, Robert\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2020\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781612198569/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781612198569/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781612198569/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781612198569\",\"1612198562\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Federal Reserve Banks\",\"Monetary Policy -- United States\",\"Economics -- United States\"],\"groupKey\":\"money_from_nothing_or_why_we_should_stop_worrying_about_debt_and_learn_to_love_the_federal_reserve�hockett_robert�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1671468\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":false,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1671468\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"OTHER\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":1,\"totalCopies\":2,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"AVAILABLE_IN_BRANCH\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"AVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1810678\":{\"id\":\"S114C1810678\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1810678\",\"title\":\"Networking All-in-one for Dummies\",\"subtitle\":\"\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"004.6 LOW\",\"description\":\"\\\"The essentials you need to learn about networking--10 books in one! With over 900 pages of clear and trustworthy information, Networking All-in-One For Dummies is the perfect beginner's guide AND the perfect professional reference book. Small networks, large networks, business networks, cloud networks--it's all covered. Learn how to set up a network and keep it functioning, using Windows Server, Linux, and related technologies. This book also covers best practices for security, managing mobile devices, and beyond. Maybe you're just getting started with networking, or maybe you know what you're doing and need a resource with all the knowledge in one place. Either way, you've found what you need with this Dummies All-in-One Plan a network from scratch and learn how to set up all the hardware and software you'll need Find explanations and examples of important networking protocols Build remote and cloud-based networks of various sizes Administer networks with Windows Server and other versions Secure your network with penetration testing and planning for cybersecurity incident responses Every network administrator needs a copy of Networking All-in-One For Dummies, the comprehensive learning resource and reliable desk reference\\\"-- Provided by publisher.\",\"genreForm\":[\"Handbooks and Manuals\",\"Handbooks and manuals\"],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Computer networks\",\"Computer networks Management\"],\"authors\":[\"Lowe, Doug\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2025\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781394278381/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781394278381/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9781394278381/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9781394278381\",\"1394278381\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[{\"name\":\"--For dummies\",\"volume\":null,\"sortName\":\"--for dummies\",\"volumeNumber\":null}],\"edition\":\"9th edition\",\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Computer Networks\",\"Computer Networks -- Management\",\"Handbooks and Manuals\"],\"groupKey\":\"networking_all_in_1_for_dummies�lowe_doug�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1810678\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":true,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1810678\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"OTHER\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":2,\"totalCopies\":3,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"AVAILABLE_IN_BRANCH\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"AVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1730913\":{\"id\":\"S114C1730913\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1730913\",\"title\":\"Parenting With An Accent\",\"subtitle\":\"How Immigrants Honor Their Heritage, Navigate Setbacks, and Chart New Paths for Their Children\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"306.874097 RUM\",\"description\":\"\\\"A candid portrait of the realities, challenges, and joys many contemporary immigrants confront while raising a new generation of Americans\\\"-- Provided by publisher.\",\"genreForm\":[\"Cross-cultural Studies\"],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Parenthood United States Cross-cultural studies\",\"Children of immigrants United States\",\"Immigrants Family relationships United States\",\"Immigrant families United States\"],\"authors\":[\"Rumer, Masha\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2022\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780807021873/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780807021873/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780807021873/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9780807021873\",\"9780807021941\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Parenthood -- United States -- Cross-cultural Studies\",\"Children of Immigrants -- United States\",\"Immigrants -- Family Relationships -- United States\",\"Immigrant Families -- United States\"],\"groupKey\":\"parenting_with_an_accent_how_immigrants_honor_their_heritage_navigate_setbacks_and_chart_new_paths_f�rumer_masha�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1730913\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":false,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1730913\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"OTHER\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":1,\"totalCopies\":2,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"AVAILABLE_IN_BRANCH\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"AVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1786566\":{\"id\":\"S114C1786566\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1786566\",\"title\":\"Slow Productivity\",\"subtitle\":\"\",\"format\":\"PLAYAWAY_AUDIOBOOK\",\"superFormats\":[\"AUDIOBOOKS_SPOKEN_WORD\",\"TALKING_BOOKS\",\"SPECIALTY_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"LISTEN\",\"callNumber\":\"PLWY 331.118 NEW\",\"description\":\"Our current definition of \\\"productivity\\\" is broken. It pushes us to treat busyness as a proxy for useful effort, leading to impossibly lengthy task lists and ceaseless meetings. Were overwhelmed by all we have to do and on the edge of burnout, left to decide between giving into soul-sapping hustle culture or rejecting ambition altogether. But are these really our only choices? Long before the arrival of pinging inboxes and clogged schedules, historys most creative and impactful philosophers, scientists, artists, and writers mastered the art of producing valuable work with staying power. In this timely and provocative book, Cal Newport harnesses the wisdom of these traditional knowledge workers to radically transform our modern jobs. Drawing from deep research on the habits and mindsets of a varied cast of storied thinkers -- from Galileo and Isaac Newton, to Jane Austen and Georgia O'Keefe -- Newport lays out the key principles of \\\"slow productivity,\\\" a more sustainable alternative to the aimless overwhelm that defines our current moment. Combining cultural criticism with systematic pragmatism, Newport deconstructs the absurdities inherent in standard notions of productivity, and then provides step-by-step advice for cultivating a slower, more humane alternative. From the aggressive rethinking of workload management, to introducing seasonal variation, to shifting your performance toward long-term quality, Slow Productivity provides a roadmap for escaping overload and arriving instead at a more timeless approach to pursuing meaningful accomplishment. The world of work is due for a new revolution. Slow productivity is exactly what we need.\",\"genreForm\":[\"Audiobooks\",\"Playaway\"],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Labor productivity\",\"Humanism\"],\"authors\":[\"Newport, Cal\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2024\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9798822682641/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9798822682641/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9798822682641/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9798822682641\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"NONFICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Labor Productivity\",\"Humanism\",\"Audiobooks\",\"Playaway\"],\"groupKey\":\"slow_productivity�newport_cal�text_eng\",\"id\":\"S114C1786566\",\"rating\":{}},\"policy\":{\"materialType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"provider\":\"ILS\",\"holdable\":true,\"itemLevelHoldableItems\":false,\"materialPolicy\":{\"supportsBatchVolumeHolds\":true,\"itemLevelHoldsPredetermined\":false,\"requiresDuration\":false,\"requiresEmailDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringHold\":false,\"requiresFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsDownload\":false,\"supportsFastAvailability\":false,\"supportsReadNow\":false,\"showFormatDuringHold\":false,\"showFormatDuringCheckout\":false,\"supportsSuspendHold\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldStartDateEdit\":false,\"supportsSuspendHoldEndDateEdit\":true,\"showQuickstartLink\":false,\"supportsBorrowingHistory\":false,\"borrowingHistorySupportsReturnedDates\":true,\"maintainsBorrowingHistoryOnDisable\":false,\"supportsCancelledExpiredHolds\":true,\"helpUrl\":null,\"quickStartUrl\":null,\"healthy\":true,\"externalAPI\":false}},\"availability\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1786566\",\"bibType\":\"PHYSICAL\",\"availabilityLocationType\":\"NA\",\"status\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"circulationType\":\"REQUEST\",\"libraryUseOnly\":false,\"heldCopies\":0,\"availableCopies\":0,\"totalCopies\":2,\"onOrderCopies\":0,\"volumesCount\":0,\"localisedStatus\":\"UNAVAILABLE\",\"eresourceDescription\":null,\"eresourceUrl\":null,\"singleBranch\":false,\"statusType\":\"UNAVAILABLE\"}},\"S114C1755945\":{\"id\":\"S114C1755945\",\"sourceLibId\":114,\"briefInfo\":{\"metadataId\":\"S114C1755945\",\"title\":\"What Child Is This?\",\"subtitle\":\"A Sherlock Holmes Christmas Adventure\",\"format\":\"BK\",\"superFormats\":[\"BOOKS\",\"MODERN_FORMATS\"],\"consumptionFormat\":\"READ\",\"callNumber\":\"MACBIRD, B\",\"description\":\"It's the season of peace and goodwill, but a Victorian Christmas is no holiday for the world's most popular detective in this new book from Bonnie MacBird, author of the bestselling Sherlock Holmes novel Art in the Blood. It's Christmastime in London, and Sherlock Holmes takes on two cases. The angelic three-year-old child of a wealthy couple is the target of a vicious kidnapper, and a country aristocrat worries that his handsome, favourite son has mysteriously vanished from his London pied à terre. Holmes and Watson, aided by the colourful Heffie O'Malley, slip slide in the ice to ensure a merry Christmas is had by nearly everybody.\",\"genreForm\":[\"Detective and mystery fiction\",\"Christmas Fiction\",\"Detective and Mystery Fiction\",\"Fiction\",\"Christmas fiction\"],\"subjectHeadings\":[\"Holmes, Sherlock Fiction\",\"Watson, John H. (Fictitious character) Fiction\",\"Private investigators England London Fiction\",\"Kidnapping Fiction\",\"Missing persons Fiction\"],\"authors\":[\"MacBird, Bonnie\"],\"publicationDate\":\"2022\",\"jacket\":{\"type\":\"SYNDETICS\",\"small\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780008521318/SC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"medium\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780008521318/MC.GIF&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"large\":\"https://secure.syndetics.com/index.aspx?isbn=9780008521318/LC.JPG&client=dougp&type=xw12&oclc=\",\"local_url\":null},\"isbns\":[\"9780008521318\",\"000852131X\",\"9780008521288\",\"000852128X\"],\"primaryLanguage\":\"eng\",\"series\":[{\"name\":\"Sherlock Holmes adventure\",\"volume\":null,\"sortName\":\"sherlock holmes adventure\",\"volumeNumber\":null}],\"edition\":null,\"multiscriptTitle\":null,\"multiscriptAuthor\":null,\"contentType\":\"FICTION\",\"audiences\":[\"ADULT\"],\"compositeSubjectHeadings\":[\"Holmes, Sherlock -- Fiction\",\"Watson, John H. (Fictitious Character) -- Fiction\",\"Private Investig